; The reserved Anim extension: hand-keyed motion for a stone whose real trajectory physics cannot reproduce.
; Readers that do not implement Anim ignore the line and replay from @ (layer 3) or v= (layer 4). Positions are fictional.
[PCN "1.0"]
[Event "Example"]
[Red "Red"]
[Yellow "Yellow"]
[Ends "8"]
[LSFE "Red"]
[Result "*"]
[Curation "reenacted"]

End 1 hammer=R
1 Y F>4
@ Y-0.02,3.50*
2 R D>4
@ Y-0.02,3.50 R0.30,0.40*
3 Y T<3
@ Y-0.02,3.50 Y0.55,-0.60*
4 R D<4
@ Y-0.02,3.50 Y0.55,-0.60 R-0.10,0.20*
5 Y G>4
@ Y-0.02,3.50 Y0.55,-0.60 R-0.10,0.20 Y-0.45,2.80*
6 R T>4
@ Y-0.02,3.50 R-0.10,0.20 Y-0.45,2.80 R0.70,-0.90*
7 Y D<3
@ Y-0.02,3.50 R-0.10,0.20 Y-0.45,2.80 R0.70,-0.90 Y0.15,-0.25*
8 R T<2
@ Y-0.02,3.50 R-0.10,0.20 Y-0.45,2.80 R0.70,-0.90 R0.90,-1.60*
; Y0 is the thrown stone; keyframes are normalised time 0..1, dur= gives the real duration in seconds.
; The unusual curl in the last metre could not be reproduced by the engine, so it is keyed by hand.
; The double take-out removes R-0.10,0.20 and R0.70,-0.90; stones without an Anim line stay where they are.
9 Y S>3
Anim Y0 dur=2.4 0:0.10,30.8 0.5:0.30,4.0 0.8:0.55,0.8 1:0.45,-0.1
@ Y-0.02,3.50 Y-0.45,2.80 R0.90,-1.60 Y0.45,-0.10*
